# ThreadSanitizer suppressions — VENDORED code only.
#
# libresidfp builds its filter lookup tables on worker threads at first SID
# instantiation (see the note in CLAUDE.md about the WASM path building them
# sequentially instead). TSan flags a race inside those builders. It is
# upstream, third-party, and reached by every test that constructs a Memory —
# so without this file the thread sanitizer aborts on essentially the whole
# suite and reports nothing about POM1's own code.
#
# That is the real cost: a job that is red for a reason nobody can act on is a
# job nobody reads, and the races it exists to catch (emulation thread × render
# thread × audio callback) never get looked at. Suppress the vendored noise so
# the signal is POM1's.
#
# Keep this list minimal and third-party ONLY. Never add a POM1 symbol here —
# a race in our code is a bug to fix, not to silence.
race:reSIDfp::FilterModelConfig
race:reSIDfp::FilterModelConfig8580
race:reSIDfp::FilterModelConfig6581

# Belt and braces: match anything coming out of the vendored tree, whatever
# the symbol is called. TSan matches this pattern against the function, file
# and library name of the frame.
race:third_party/libresidfp
